Test vectors for Cocoon's Spaces primitives (space/), generated by running the
reference implementation as published for the November 12, 2026 alpha:

  packages: @atproto/space and @atproto/crypto 0.0.0-spaces-alpha-20261112204144
  source:   https://github.com/bluesky-social/atproto
            branch permissioned-data-alpha, commit d4def6e9f521896ed8222f576d54923d00b5fbeb

gen-vectors.mjs (in this directory, with re-run instructions in its header)
writes all five files with fixed keys, after checking each vector with the
reference itself:

  vectors.json  set hashes, commit and record MACs and their headers, KEM
                encapsulations (key share and shared secret against a fixed
                #atproto_kem key), credential request signatures, and tokens
  export.star   a space repo as the reference's writeRepoStar writes it for
                getRepo (STAR, atproto-space-repo profile), five records, one
                naming a blob
  export.json   that repo's commit, the shared secret and MAC headers it was
                served with, and its records
  meta.star     a space meta archive as writeSpaceMetaStar writes it for
                exportSpaceMeta (memberspace policy, two members, two writers)
  meta.json     its contents

Signatures, token jtis and KEM key shares are random, so a re-run changes only
those values (and the export's MAC header).

The HTTP signature, token, MAC, KEM and STAR test cases (space/*_test.go) are
ported from packages/space/src/{http-signature,star,space-meta-archive}.test.ts
and packages/space/tests/{credential,mac,kem,sync,repo-commit}.test.ts at the
same commit. kem_test.go also checks the export-only DHKEM(P-256) HPKE vector
from packages/space/tests/kem.test.ts.

License: MIT (bluesky-social/atproto).

Since the October 22 alpha the vectors changed shape: commit and record MACs
are HTTP message signature headers, KEM encapsulations come with their
Accept-Signature requests, STAR archives carry control bytes, and meta.star /
meta.json are a space meta archive written by writeSpaceMetaStar.

star-valid-fixtures.json and star-invalid-fixtures.json are the DASL-STAR
interop fixtures from https://tangled.org/microcosm.blue/star (interop/, at
41bdec1fd1be7f6f30a1f961a01442b2fa2ec3c1), run by space/star_interop_test.go.
